=== Honesty note ===
Apple sources cross-compile on this Windows host (compileKotlin/compileTestKotlin for iosSimulatorArm64 + macosArm64 SUCCESSFUL),
but Apple unit tests cannot EXECUTE on Windows: iosSimulatorArm64Test / macosArm64Test are SKIPPED (Kotlin/Native test execution
requires a macOS host). The Keychain RUNTIME behaviour of AppleKeychainTokenStore must therefore be validated on macOS CI. All
shared/auth logic that can run on Windows is exercised by the Android local JVM run of commonTest (MockEngine + AuthBrowser fake +
in-memory SecureTokenStore), which is green. The Android Keystore actual likewise needs on-device/instrumented validation; its
commonTest coverage uses the in-memory fake. AuthBrowser has no shared implementation by design (platform W4/A4/P5 own the redirect UI).
Design realization: the spec's "SecureTokenStore expect/actual" is realized as a commonMain INTERFACE with
platform implementations (AndroidKeystoreTokenStore, AppleKeychainTokenStore) injected from the platform app
modules, rather than a literal `expect class` + `actual` factory — the Android Keystore store needs a Context that
a parameterless actual factory cannot supply. Same secure-enclave contract, same {common,android,apple}Main/auth
file layout the spec specifies; commonTest uses the in-memory fake (InMemorySecureTokenStore) as required.

